// Template for the local secrets file. It is committed as guidance; the file that
// actually feeds the build is `Secrets.local.xcconfig` (git-ignored), which you create
// by copying this one and filling in your RevenueCat key:
//
//     cp App/Secrets.xcconfig.example App/Secrets.local.xcconfig
//     # then edit App/Secrets.local.xcconfig and paste your key after the equals sign.
//
// A blank value means the app builds and runs fully free: RevenueCat is never configured,
// the paywall surfaces its "offering unavailable" state, and nothing crashes (spec §6.2 is
// what a keyless build exercises — see `scripts/m9-manual-qa.md` §2).
//
// `project.yml` reads this as `$(SALUS_REVENUECAT_API_KEY)` on the app target, and the
// value flows into `ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment` for `SalusApp.init` to read.
SALUS_REVENUECAT_API_KEY =
